  "decision_conditions": [
    "The rating level of the noise emitted from the extractor flue/ducting equipment shall be lower than the existing background noise level by at least 5dB(A) as measured from the&amp;nbsp;nearest noise sensitive premises, with all machinery operating together at maximum capacity.&amp;nbsp; The measurements and assessment shall be made according to BS 4142:1990.",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans: Site Location Plan; Drawing Numbers 032.25/01,&amp;nbsp;032.25/02,&amp;nbsp;032.25/03,&amp;nbsp;032.25/04,&amp;nbsp; 032.25/05,&amp;nbsp;032.25/06,&amp;nbsp;032.25/07,&amp;nbsp;032.25/08,&amp;nbsp;032.25/09,&amp;nbsp;032.25/10,&amp;nbsp;032.25/11.&amp;nbsp;",
    "The development hereby approved shall be installed and operated in accordance with the recommendations contained in the Noise Assessment Report provided in support of the application, prepared by Ned Johnson Acoustic Consultants Limited (Document reference&amp;nbsp;622324), dated the 21st April 2024. Any required noise mitigation measures required to comply with the recommendations shall be installed and maintained in perpetuity.&amp;nbsp;",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Any plant and machinery, including that for fume extraction, ventilation, refrigeration and air conditioning, which may be used by reason of granting this permission, shall be so installed, used and thereafter retained as to prevent the transmission of unreasonable noise, vibration, and odour/fume into any neighbouring premises."
